    ct:CDISC%20Definition "A measurement of the neutralizing cross-reactive binding antidrug antibody in a biological specimen. A neutralizing cross-reactive binding antidrug antibody is a type of ADA that binds to an endogenous molecule that is structurally similar to an analogue test article and diminishes or negates its function." ;
