<https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/id/sdtm-ct/SDTM%20Terminology/C160922/C161338>
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/sdtm-ct#SDTM%20Terminology> ;
    ct:CDISC%20Definition "A mathematical formula to estimate glomerular filtration rate that takes into account sex, age, race, and serum creatinine (SCr). eGFR(mL/min/1.73 m2)=141 x min(SCr/k, 1)^a x max(SCr/k, 1)^-1.209 x 0.993^Age x 1.018 [if female] x 1.159 [if black] where: SCr is in mg/dL; k=0.7 for Female and 0.9 for Male; a=-0.329 for female and -0.411 for male. (Levey AS, Stevens LA, Schmid CH, Zhang YL, Castro AF, Feldman HI, Kusek JW, Eggers P, Van Lente F, Greene T. A new equation to estimate glomerular filtration rate. Ann Intern Med. 2009;150:604-612.)" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Submission%20Value "CKD-EPI CREATININE FORMULA" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Synonym%28s%29 "CKD-EPI Creatinine 2009 Formula" ;
    ct:Code "C161338" ;
    ct:Codelist%20Code "C160922" ;
    ct:Codelist%20Name "Laboratory Analytical Method Calculation Formula" ;
    ct:NCI%20Preferred%20Term "CKD-EPI Creatinine Formula" ;
.

<https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/id/sdtm-ct/SDTM%20Terminology/C160922/C161339>
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/sdtm-ct#SDTM%20Terminology> ;
    ct:CDISC%20Definition "A mathematical formula to estimate glomerular filtration rate that takes into account sex, age, race, and serum cystatin C (Scys). eGFR(mL/min/1.73 m2)=133 x min(Scys/0.8, 1)^-0.499 x max (Scys/0.8, 1)^-1.328 x 0.996^Age x 0.932 [if female]. (Inker LA, Schmid CH, Tighiouart H, et al. Estimating glomerular filtration rate from serum creatinine and cystatin C. N Engl J Med. 2012;367(1):20-29.)" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Submission%20Value "CKD-EPI CYSTATIN C FORMULA" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Synonym%28s%29 "CKD-EPI Cystatin C 2012 Formula" ;
    ct:Code "C161339" ;
    ct:Codelist%20Code "C160922" ;
    ct:Codelist%20Name "Laboratory Analytical Method Calculation Formula" ;
    ct:NCI%20Preferred%20Term "CKD-EPI Cystatin C Formula" ;
.

<https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/id/sdtm-ct/SDTM%20Terminology/C160922/C161340>
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/sdtm-ct#SDTM%20Terminology> ;
    ct:CDISC%20Definition "A mathematical formula to estimate glomerular filtration rate that takes into account sex, age, race, serum creatinine (SCr) and serum cystatin C (Scys). eGFR(mL/min/1.73 m2)=135 x min(SCr/k, 1)a x max(SCr/k, 1)-0.601 x min(Scys/0.8, 1)-0.375 x max(Scys/0.8, 1)-0.711 x 0.995^Age x 0.969 [if female] x 1.08 [if black]. (Inker LA, Schmid CH, Tighiouart H, et al. Estimating glomerular filtration rate from serum creatinine and cystatin C. N Engl J Med. 2012;367(1):20-29.)" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Submission%20Value "CKD-EPI CREATININE-CYSTATIN C FORMULA" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Synonym%28s%29 "CKD-EPI Creatinine-Cystatin C 2012 Formula" ;
    ct:Code "C161340" ;
