    ct:CDISC%20Definition "Any antigen(s) encoded by the GAD gene that catalyze the decarboxylation of glutamate to GABA. They can be considered as autoantigens and are commonly associated with the autoimmune diseases type 1 diabetes, autoimmune polyendocrine syndrome types 1 and 2, and stiff man syndrome." ;
