    ct:CDISC%20Definition "An antigen encoded by the DPYSL5 gene that regulates neurite outgrowth and neurogenesis. It can be considered as a neuronal autoantigen and is commonly associated with autoimmune neurodegenerative disorders related to cancer, such as paraneoplastic neurologic syndrome." ;
    ct:CDISC%20Submission%20Value "CV2 ANTIGEN" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Synonym%28s%29 "Collapsin Response Mediator Protein 5; CRMP5; CV2" ;
