.

<https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/id/sdtm-ct/SDTM%20Terminology/C66737/C49688>
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/sdtm-ct#SDTM%20Terminology> ;
    ct:CDISC%20Definition "Later Phase 2 trials, in transition to Phase 3, where the study populations more closely reflect the population, dosage, and condition for intended use. [Clarification of FDA Guidance for industry end of Phase 2a meetings, September 2009; Discussion in Peter B. Gilbert. SOME DESIGN ISSUES IN PHASE 2B VERSUS PHASE 3 PREVENTION TRIALS FOR TESTING EFFICACY OF PRODUCTS OR CONCEPTS. Stat Med. 2010 May 10; 29(10): 1061-1071.]" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Submission%20Value "PHASE IIB TRIAL" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Synonym%28s%29 "2B; Trial Phase 2B" ;
    ct:Code "C49688" ;
    ct:Codelist%20Code "C66737" ;
    ct:Codelist%20Name "Trial Phase Response" ;
    ct:NCI%20Preferred%20Term "Phase IIb Trial" ;
.

<https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/id/sdtm-ct/SDTM%20Terminology/C66737/C49689>
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/sdtm-ct#SDTM%20Terminology> ;
    ct:CDISC%20Definition "Later Phase 3 trial done near the time of approval to elicit additional findings. NOTE: Dossier review may continue while associated Phase 3b trials are conducted. These trials may be required as a condition of regulatory authority approval. Phase 3a is in common usage but not reflected in regulatory guidance. (CDISC Glossary)" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Submission%20Value "PHASE IIIB TRIAL" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Synonym%28s%29 "3B; Trial Phase 3B" ;
    ct:Code "C49689" ;
    ct:Codelist%20Code "C66737" ;
    ct:Codelist%20Name "Trial Phase Response" ;
    ct:NCI%20Preferred%20Term "Phase IIIb Trial" ;
.

<https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/id/sdtm-ct/SDTM%20Terminology/C66737/C54721>
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/sdtm-ct#SDTM%20Terminology> ;
    ct:CDISC%20Definition "First-in-human trials, in a small number of subjects, that are conducted before Phase 1 trials and are intended to assess new candidate therapeutic and imaging agents. The study agent is administered at a low dose for a limited time, and there is no therapeutic or diagnostic intent. NOTE: FDA Guidance for Industry, Investigators, and Reviewers: Exploratory IND Studies, January 2006 classifies such studies as Phase 1. NOTE: A Phase 0 study might not include any drug delivery but may be an exploration of human material from a study (e.g., tissue samples or biomarker determinations). [Improving the Quality of Cancer Clinical Trials: Workshop summary-Proceedings of the National Cancer Policy Forum Workshop, improving the Quality of Cancer Clinical Trials (Washington, DC, Oct 2007)] (CDISC glossary)" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Submission%20Value "EARLY PHASE I" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Synonym%28s%29 "0; Phase 0 Trial; Pre-clinical Trial; Trial Phase 0" ;
    ct:Code "C54721" ;
    ct:Codelist%20Code "C66737" ;
    ct:Codelist%20Name "Trial Phase Response" ;
    ct:NCI%20Preferred%20Term "Early Phase 1 Trial" ;
.

