    ct:CDISC%20Definition "An electrocardiographic finding of a junctional rhythm that arises as a physiologic response to extreme slowing or arrest of sinus node activity. In this setting, a faster junctional rhythm may be a normal response to a very slow or absent sinus rate." ;
    ct:CDISC%20Submission%20Value "JUNCTIONAL ESCAPE RHYTHM" ;
    ct:Code "C135393" ;
    ct:Codelist%20Code "C71150" ;
    ct:Codelist%20Name "ECG Result" ;
    ct:NCI%20Preferred%20Term "Junctional Escape Rhythm by ECG Finding" ;
.

