    ct:CDISC%20Definition "A muscle of the lower leg, in general extending from the middle third of the medial surface of the fibula and the adjacent interosseous membrane to the base and dorsal center of the distal phalanx of the great toe; primary function is to extend the big toe and dorsiflex the ankle." ;
