    ct:CDISC%20Definition "A system of (usually) epifluorescence light microscopy in which a fine laser beam of light is scanned over the object through the objective lens. This technique is particularly good at rejecting light from outside the plane of focus and so produces higher effective resolution than other microscopy techniques." ;
    ct:CDISC%20Submission%20Value "CONFOCAL MICROSCOPY" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Synonym%28s%29 "Confocal Laser Microscopy" ;
