    ct:CDISC%20Definition "A diagrammatic method to test visual acuity that uses a set of cards with familiar pictures placed in either the top or bottom half of the card, and which is used for those individuals who are unable to provide a verbal response to questions, including infants, toddlers, and other non-verbal individuals." ;
    ct:CDISC%20Submission%20Value "CARDIFF ACUITY CARDS" ;
