    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/sdtm-ct#SDTM%20Terminology> ;
    ct:CDISC%20Definition "A technique that measures an evoked potential caused by a visual stimulus and recorded by an electroencephalogram, and which is used for those individuals who are unable to provide a verbal response to questions, including infants, toddlers, and other non-verbal individuals." ;
    ct:CDISC%20Submission%20Value "SWEEP VISUAL EVOKED POTENTIAL" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Synonym%28s%29 "Sweep VEP" ;
