    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/sdtm-ct#SDTM%20Terminology> ;
    ct:CDISC%20Definition "An imaging technique that combines MRI with ultrasound to assess the mechanical properties of tissues. An MRI machine captures a cross sectional image of the sound waves, produced by ultrasound techniques, which are then processed by computer to produce an image showing the hardness or elasticity of tissues within the cross section." ;
    ct:CDISC%20Submission%20Value "MAGNETIC RESONANCE ELASTOGRAPHY" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Synonym%28s%29 "MRE" ;
