    ct:CDISC%20Definition "Any type of computer-assisted microscopy that uses digital imaging and software to classify and quantify particles. This enables objective, reproducible evaluation by applying algorithms to detect the presence of entities such as protein aggregates, cell counts, and other morphological information." ;
