    ct:CDISC%20Definition "A functional magnetic resonance imaging technique that uses the difference between the magnetic signals of hemoglobin when it is carrying oxygen (oxyhemoglobin) and when it is not carrying oxygen (deoxyhemoglobin) to detect metabolic activity, and hence neurologic activity, in the brain. (NCI)" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Submission%20Value "BLOOD OXYGEN LEVEL-DEPENDENT FUNCTIONAL MRI" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Synonym%28s%29 "Blood Oxygen Level-Dependent fMRI; BOLD fMRI" ;
