    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/sdtm-ct#SDTM%20Terminology> ;
    ct:CDISC%20Definition "A bipolar electrocardiogram limb lead which records the voltage between the positive electrode near the apex of the heart (located in the ICS of left 5-6 rib close to the sternum) and the negative electrode behind the right ear near the right mastoid process." ;
    ct:CDISC%20Submission%20Value "LEAD AXIAL" ;
    ct:Code "C135390" ;
    ct:Codelist%20Code "C90013" ;
