    ct:CDISC%20Definition "A scoring system used to measure metastatic response to therapy using 123I-metaiodobenzylguanidine scintigraphy, in which 10 regions of the body are scored. (Ady N, Zucker JM, Asselain B, Edeline V, Bonnin F, Michon J, Gongora R, Manil L. A new 123I-MIBG whole body scan scoring method--application to the prediction of the response of metastases to induction chemotherapy in stage IV neuroblastoma. Eur J Cancer. 1995;31A(2):256-61.; Matthay KK, Edeline V, Lumbroso J, Tanguy ML, Asselain B, Zucker JM, Valteau-Couanet D, Hartmann O, Michon J. Correlation of early metastatic response by 123I-metaiodobenzylguanidine scintigraphy with overall response and event-free survival in stage IV neuroblastoma. J Clin Oncol. 2003 Jul 1;21(13):2486-91.)" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Submission%20Value "Curie Absolute Score" ;
    ct:CDISC%20Synonym%28s%29 "Curie Absolute Score; Curie Score" ;
    ct:Code "C133462" ;
    ct:Codelist%20Code "C96778" ;
    ct:Codelist%20Name "Tumor or Lesion Properties Test Name" ;
    ct:NCI%20Preferred%20Term "Curie Scoring System" ;
.

